+## The error path
+
+- A throw from `beforeSession` reaches the same `catch` and `finally` as any other failure in the turn: the caller still sees the same rejection, `onError` fires with the thrown error in its usual `(session, error)` shape, and `afterSession` runs ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
+- `afterSession` therefore fires for a turn that never began, and nothing in its arguments distinguishes that from a completed turn: a hook can assume no user input was rewritten, no provider call was made and the turn wrote no entry of its own, so a deployer who must tell the two apart tracks it in its own state rather than reading it off the session ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
